Loading data
phibble builds tables from CSV files, PDO queries, query builders, and PHP arrays:
$schools = DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv');
$rows = DataFrame::fromRows([['id' =&gt; 1, 'x' =&gt; 2.5], ['id' =&gt; 2, 'x' =&gt; null]]);
$cols = DataFrame::fromColumns(['id' =&gt; [1, 2], 'x' =&gt; [2.5, null]]);
null is a missing value, R’s NA. A DataFrame is immutable, so every function returns a new table and leaves its input unchanged. echo $table prints the first rows in the format of R’s tibble package.

Columns, row closures, and vector helpers
Columns are named with strings: 'score' where dplyr takes a bare score.
A row closure is an ordinary PHP closure. It receives the row as a Phibble\Row, whose columns read as $r-&gt;score or $r['score'], and the table of the row’s group as a second argument:
mutate(gap: fn ($r) =&gt; $r-&gt;score - $r-&gt;prior_score)
filter(fn ($r, $group) =&gt; $r-&gt;score &gt; mean('score')($group))
A vector helper is one of phplyr’s functions for whole columns, such as lag('x'), cumsum('x'), min_rank('x'), or mean('x'). It is evaluated once per group. A summary helper in mutate() gives one value per group, and that value is repeated on every row of the group:

PHP 8.5+PHP 8.3–8.4


$schools = DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv') |&gt; group_by('school');

echo json_encode([
    'groups' =&gt; $schools |&gt; group_vars(),
    'n_groups' =&gt; $schools |&gt; n_groups(),
    'sizes' =&gt; \array_slice($schools |&gt; group_size(), 0, 4),
]), "\n\n";

// Grouped mutate: helpers are evaluated within each group.
echo $schools |&gt;
    mutate(centered: fn ($r, $g) =&gt; round($r-&gt;score - mean('score')($g), 2), rank_in_school: min_rank(desc('score'))) |&gt;
    ungroup() |&gt;
    head(4);

// One table per group.
$parts = $schools |&gt; group_split();
echo "\n", \count($parts), ' tables; the first has ', $parts[0]-&gt;nrow(), " rows\n";


$schools = phplyr(DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv'))-&gt;groupBy('school')-&gt;get();

echo json_encode([
    'groups' =&gt; phplyr($schools)-&gt;groupVars(),
    'n_groups' =&gt; phplyr($schools)-&gt;nGroups(),
    'sizes' =&gt; \array_slice(phplyr($schools)-&gt;groupSize(), 0, 4),
