Function
Rows




slice(1, 3), slice(-1)
By 1-based position; negative positions drop rows.


slice_head(n:), slice_tail(n:)
The first or last rows.


slice_min(x, n:), slice_max(x, n:)
The rows with the smallest or largest values, with ties kept unless withTies: false.


slice_sample(n:, replace:, weightBy:)
Random rows. Seed with mt_srand().


head(n)
The first rows of the whole table, ignoring groups.


